From dd773d7211515d5f5ffaee28681ff4ecaeba56e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 22:26:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] feat(crew): daemon liveness watchdog for opt-in crews +
 rig status surface (feryn-409i)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A crew session (e.g. the iris PR-review crew) can transition to 'stopped'
silently — parking ALL reviews and merges until a human notices. There was no
crew liveness watchdog (only witness/refinery are supervised) and crew health
wasn't surfaced anywhere. Because a stopped crew is indistinguishable from a
deliberate `gt crew stop` (crew liveness is derived purely from tmux presence),
auto-restart is opt-in so the daemon never fights an intentional stop.

  - Add an AutoRestart flag to CrewWorker (persisted in crew state), toggled via
    `gt crew autorestart <name> on|off`. Off by default.
  - Daemon heartbeat step (after refineries) restarts AutoRestart crews whose
    session has died, across operational rigs — modeled on ensureWitnessRunning:
    reuses getPatrolRigs (operational gate), honors the restartTracker
    crash-loop / backoff guards, and is pressure-gated (a restart spawns a
    Claude session). Crews without the flag are never touched.
  - Surface crew liveness as a first-class health signal in `gt rig ls`:
    "Crew: N (X running, Y stopped)" plus a warning line listing any
    auto-restart crew whose session is currently down (JSON gains crew_running /
    crew_stopped / crew_supervised_down).

Tests: SetAutoRestart persistence round-trip through Get/List; unknown-crew
error. Watchdog mirrors the established, tested witness/refinery restart path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
